       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Dose:** 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. The maximum labeled daily dose of ibuprofen for adults is 3,200 mg/day, so this is twice the limit.\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is also twice the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg.\n- **Risks:** Doses this high raise the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't remove that risk.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg by mouth, four times daily** (3,200 mg/day). This is the maximum for anti-inflammatory dosing.\n- **400\u2013800 mg by mouth every 6\u20138 hours as needed.** This is typical for pain or fever.\n- **1600 mg total per day,** divided into smaller doses, for example 400 mg four times daily.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it. If 1600 mg four times daily is intentional, please confirm that and give the clinical rationale. I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
      }
